      "weather": "FINE",
      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FUNNYIFITWON (3) is the one to beat after going under by only half a length to Tokyo Bandit at this track last start, with a slow beginning and a hold-up near the 150m adding merit to the effort. The rise to 1600m carries some query, but he has won around the trip before. On top. MIAMI BABY (2) is the obvious danger, having beaten BIDEN TIME at this venue two starts ago before closing off from the rear in a BM76. His track record and one win from two at the distance keep him firmly in the winning mix. BIDEN TIME (1) was plain late in the same BM76, but his previous second to Kessler and solid record at this track and distance give him genuine place appeal. HELL AND BACK (4) has been freshened since making late ground behind MIAMI BABY, though his unplaced 1600m record at this venue keeps him a rung below the main pair.",
